KNOWNBUG
wire_array_2d1.sv
--aig --bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The netlist converter leaves the definitions of the elements of a
two-dimensional array unsplit, and the elements read by them are then on
a cycle, and unconstrained. p0 is refuted. This is sound, but less precise
than word-level BMC.
